[Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  ladies and gentlemen dear conference  members  thank you very much for giving  me in this conference who focus so much  on technical solutions  and excellent communication a window of  solidarity  to humanitarian crisis caused by the  awful war in the ukraine  we heard this very personal statement  and i'm sure you could speak much better  than me about the effects to your family  and your friends so i only will give the  speech as a austrian staying in austria  but being in touch with many people in  the ukraine and trying to organize help  to them  so many people  lost their futures within the first  moments  this war started a nightmare for so many  but it also shows us a lot of solidarity  here in europe  i'm personally touched by the phone  calls with my colleagues in the ukraine  who are sitting in an air ride shelter  while being on phone or laptop and  coordinating help  our colleagues who evacuate whole  orphanages overnight and organize still  children use groups  where it is needed  our project partners who stay shoulder  and shoulder with volunteers to read  back food medical devices or other  needed goods to distribute them to  people in destroyed villages and cities  i admire all the groups of people who  welcome arriving refugees day and night  at the border and host and serve them  later in their private homes  so many people spend their time over  their infrastructures and often risk  life to help others  our austrian-based ngo huge dynavelt  doesn't leave these people alone our  network of dombosco organizes its active  about 80 countries around the world we  support community development programs  schools street children programs as well  as educational and technical training  courses in countries of the so-called  global south  education overcomes poverty is what we  believe and work to promote it  in the event of a humanitarian crisis or  a war like now in ukraine we do  everything we can to stand with our  experienced partners and friends  our tombosco partners  we mainly cooperate with are usually  active on the spots since many decades  ready to act in any moment  they know the local conditions and they  rely on the large number of volunteers  even now  our human eval networks maintains 12  locations within the ukraine and many  others along the borders like in poland  slovakia and the river republic of  moldova  two major centres in ukraine are  supplied by us with essentials for  people in the area  at in the beginning it was leaf lamborgh  and recently there is a growing concern  that the situation in odessa is getting  worse  drugs regularly bring relief goods  across the border to supply the centers  with the most needed material  about 200 employees are still working in  the facilities in ukraine which are  supported by many volunteers during this  difficult hours  they all decided to stay in a dangerous  environment to help  gunfire as we heard bombs syrians  uncertainty  what comes up accompanies them  i was touched when i heard  how tons of bread is being packed day by  day in live and brought inland by train  and cars to be distributed to other  centers  however what we offer is not only  materialistic things or financial aid to  people in need  but what is much more important for  people is that they know they are not  left alone  it is important that people connect with  them and accompany them on their first  escape or welcome them later in safe  neighbor countries  our local partners within the ukraine  risk their life to ensure that others  receive the help they need  i am so grateful that still so many  motivated people from our network are  offering guidance and assistance  and i'm very grateful for every  financial support we receive as ngo to  help the people of the ukraine now and  tomorrow  this crisis will not end soon you said  it already it will become worse create  also other crises like hunger crisis in  countries far away who in the future  will not get the expected amount of corn  from the one of the worldwide leading  exporters of this living spending good  we and many other ngos working in the  so-called hunger countries already fear  the situation of lack of food and  prepare us for what could come as much  as possible  but what we need would be food  four weeks ago i visited our educational  programs in ecuador  even there people are dealing with the  effects of this war especially bananas  and roses from ecuador can not longer be  sold to crime and russia  and  workers from the farms there are losing  their jobs and their only income  this war has also an impact to the most  remote corners to the world  but we also feel a heartbreaking  international solidarity of our partners  only one example  the community farmers in one of our  small agricultural farms in uganda came  together and decided as a village to  sell one of the few cows they have and  donate the money to help the ukraine war  refugees what an example  i'm very grateful to our donors  foundations and companies with their  support  they show us and they motivate us to not  leave behind people in need  dear conference participants please  become also partner of our humanitarian  aid program  if you are not already engaged in others  or support andre who need really the  staff to improve and  to improve the network he has  please help also in the humanitarian  sector and if you do not have any  resources to spend  perhaps you have also such a good like a  cow you could sell and spend the capture  you get  while i'm standing on the stage a big  truck with life spending goods is being  loaded and will be on his way to odessa  soon your contribution make this  possible and made others activities too  several of my colleagues are there on  our stand as we heard please come and  visit us we will give more information  on what we are doing  i hope to see you there and stay healthy  optimistic and stay and enjoy your stay  in vienna life goes on  [Applause]  [Music]  so  [Music]  you

